invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply-gcc.sh
reason: ct_widemul_s corrects the high word once for each negative
  operand through a mask of that operand's sign bit. Written as two ifs
  on the signs, clang lowers both back to the mask and the clang gate's
  count does not move, so that gate passes this; every gcc emits two
  branches on the signs where x25519 inlines the routine -- two IT
  blocks on the Cortex-M3, two bgez on mips32r2, two bge on rv32 -- and
  x25519.c goes two over its ceiling under each gcc spec. The Arm gcc
  is the one lint-wide-multiply-gcc resolves without docker, so it is
  the catch target; test/docker-mips.sh and test/docker-riscv32.sh
  object the same way (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/141).

--- old
    uint32_t ma = (uint32_t)(a >> 31);
    uint32_t mb = (uint32_t)(b >> 31);
    uint32_t hi = (uint32_t)(p >> 32) - (ub & ma) - (ua & mb);
--- new
    uint32_t hi = (uint32_t)(p >> 32);
    if (a < 0) {
        hi -= ub;
    }
    if (b < 0) {
        hi -= ua;
    }
